==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|знати}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*znati}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*źnōˀtei}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*ǵnéh₃t||to know, get to know}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}. Cognates include {{cog|pl|znać}}, {{cog|en|know}}, {{m|en|kenning}}, {{m|en|canny}}, {{cog|de|kennen}} and {{cog|sa|ज्ञा||to know}}.

For the collective noun sense of "nobility, aristocratic people", itself derived from the verb знать. It became the root for {{l|ru|зна́тный}}, referring to noble people being known for their higher status in medieval Russian society.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
** {{audio|ru|Ru-знать.ogg}}
* {{IPA|ru|[znat͡sʲ]|a=Belarus}} (''phonetic respelling'': знаць)
* {{rhymes|ru|atʲ|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|знать|impf|pf=узна́ть|vn=зна́ние}}

# to [[know]]: to be familiar with or accustomed to a person, place, or thing
#: {{w|Russian Synodal Bible}}, Mark 4.11:
#* {{quote|ru|И сказал им: вам дано '''знать''' тайны Царствия Божия, а тем внешним все бывает в притчах;|t=He answered them, “The mystery of the kingdom of God has been granted to you. But to those outside everything comes in parables,}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[её]] [[хорошо́]] '''зна́ю'''.|I '''know''' her well.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[хорошо́]] '''зна́ю''' [[математика|матема́тику]].|I '''know''' math well.}}
# to [[know]]: to be in possession of a specific fact or datum
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] '''зна́ю''', [[где]] [[он]] [[жить|живёт]].|I '''know''' where he lives.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] '''зна́ю''', [[ско́лько]] [[два]] [[плюс]] [[два]].|I '''know''' how much two plus two is.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[не]] '''зна́ю''', [[когда́]] [[этот|э́то]] [[быть|бы́ло]].|I don’t '''know''' when it was.}}

